# 🏗️ Main Project

## TeamFlow — Project & Team Operations Platform

TeamFlow is a backend platform that helps organizations manage teams and projects.

The system allows users to:

* Create and manage organizations
* Create teams
* Manage team members
* Create projects
* Manage project members
* Create and assign tasks
* Track task progress
* Organize tasks into sprints
* Add labels and comments
* Define task dependencies
* Track work time
* Receive notifications
* Search and analyze project data
* Use an AI assistant to understand project information

The project grows throughout all six sprints.

> **Important:** The learner does not build six separate projects. Every sprint extends, refactors, or improves the same TeamFlow system.

---

# 🧩 Core Domain

The main domain contains:

### Organization

The top-level business boundary containing teams and projects.

### Team

A group of users belonging to an organization.

### Project

A project owned by an organization and managed by project members.

### Project Member

A user participating in a project with a specific role.

### Task

A unit of work belonging to a project.

A task may have:

* Title
* Description
* Status
* Priority
* Creator
* Assignee
* Due Date
* Labels
* Dependencies
* Comments
* Time Entries

### Sprint

A time-boxed period containing project tasks.

### Task Dependency

A relationship describing that one task depends on another task.

### Comment

A discussion attached to a task.

### Time Entry

A record of time spent working on a task.

### Notification

A message generated by important system events.

### Activity

A record of important actions performed inside the system.

